REVIVE p_de90

=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_7a3e — Cooking at 19:00; water bottle desk-to-sink-to-table cycle (fork of p_2d6e)

Marco runs 6:30–7:15 before work on weekdays (untested; shoes at shoe_rack at 03:00 every day, no robot patrol during the run window). Both work from home 9:00–17:30. The key correction from the parent (p_2d6e): the cooking window is 19:00–20:30, not 18:30–19:30. The pan is at cupboard_k1 at 18:00 and at counter_k1 at 19:00; the spatula is at drawer_k_k1 at 18:00 and at counter_k1 at 19:00 (×3) and 20:00; the recipe book is at pantry_shelf_k1 at 18:00 and at counter_k1 at 19:00. Cooking clearly begins at 19:00. The parent's 18:5–19:5 window caught the transition, not the cooking itself, and its pan claim went against 3 times since the last call.

The second correction: Marco's water bottle follows a clear daily cycle. It is at desk_b1 from 08:00 to 11:00 (sightings at 08, 09×3, 10, 11×2), then disappears during the mid-day work block (no sightings 12–17; the 32 empty looks at desk_b1 during 9–17 confirm it is not visible at the desk after 11). It reappears at dish_rack_k1 at 18:00, at sink_k1 at 19:00 (being rinsed before dinner), at dining_table_d1 at 20:00 (×2, during the meal), and returns to dish_rack_k1 overnight. The parent put it at desk_b1 for the full 9–17 window, which is wrong after 11:00.

What would refute this fork: the pan at counter_k1 at 18:00 on a weekday (cooking too early), or water_bottle_marco at desk_b1 at 14:00 on a weekday (it should be at the sink or hidden).

